  "exact_prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept\nAsset type: original retro SNES RPG interface badge master, intended for exact 46 by 14 logical pixel export.\nCreate ONE horizontal compact pixel-art badge reading exactly \"LVL 1\". Genuine transparent alpha outside the badge. A small deep navy/charcoal plate with stepped rounded pixel corners, thin dark outer outline and a restrained slate upper-left bevel. Center chunky gold/amber bitmap lettering with ivory top highlights, amber lower shading and a dark one-logical-pixel outline. Uppercase L V L, a clear space, then numeral 1. Lettering is identical in scale across all glyphs, 7 logical pixels tall, approximately 5 logical pixels wide per glyph, with sturdy strokes. Badge width-to-height ratio exactly 46:14 (about 3.29:1). Design as a tiny 46x14-pixel sprite enlarged using nearest-neighbor blocks: each logical pixel should be a uniform square, hard edges only, a small deliberate palette. Plate and lettering fully visible, centered, with ample transparent margins around the badge. Simple flat 16-bit videogame UI sprite, readable at 14 pixels tall; no tiny texture, no speckle, no glow, no blur, no antialiasing, no perspective, no decorations, no other words, no logos, no third-party or Games Workshop imagery. This is the one master style from which matching LVL 2 through LVL 6 badges will be derived.",
  "originality_note": "Original artwork (built-in image generation); no third-party or GW-derived imagery.",
  "production_notes": [
    "The generated alpha silhouette was cropped at (374, 224, 1623, 548) and normalized to 46x14 with nearest-neighbor sampling.",
    "The plate alpha mask and all plate/letter palette colors are derived from the generated master.",
    "The plate bevel geometry was procedurally redrawn on the source-derived alpha mask with source-derived palette colors for a clean one-logical-pixel edge.",
    "The generated LVL lettering guided the final shapes, but the shared 5x7 LVL glyphs and numerals 1-6 were manually normalized as bitmap masks for consistent legibility.",
    "A deterministic 1-logical-pixel 8-neighbor dark outline and source-derived ivory/gold/amber row shading were applied to the normalized glyph masks.",
    "The 2x and 3x files are exact nearest-neighbor integer replications of each 46x14 logical image; no blur or antialiasing was used.",
    "The preserved generated master is unchanged and byte-identical to its source under ~/.codex/generated_images."
